+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${FULLPKGNAME} on OpenBSD
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

The `m` CLI is installed as /usr/local/bin/m, with its manual page
(man 1 m) and its project templates under
/usr/local/lib/node_modules/@pasosdejesus/m/dist/templates (the copy that
`m:create` reads, so no network is needed).

First checks:

	m --version
	m --help
	m:create myproject "description"

Requirements

Creating projects needs pnpm 11 (corepack enable pnpm).  pnpm 12 cannot be
installed on OpenBSD: it only ships per-platform binaries.

!!! DO NOT INSTALL m WITH npm AS root
!!!
!!! "doas npm i -g @pasosdejesus/m" writes to /usr/local, the same tree
!!! pkg_add owns: it overwrites bin/m and lib/node_modules/@pasosdejesus/m.
!!! From then on the package cannot be accounted for: pkg_check reports
!!! "couldn't read packing-list", pkg_delete does not clean it up and
!!! pkg_add -u may mix the port's files with npm's.

For a version newer than the port, use a user copy:

	m m:self-update        # installs into ~/.m-cli
	# keep ~/.bin before /usr/local/bin in PATH

A recent m prefers the newest managed copy (and says which one it uses) and
never runs a copy owned by another user.  For a one-off: npx @pasosdejesus/m.

If you already installed it with npm as root, restore the package:

	doas npm uninstall -g @pasosdejesus/m
	doas pkg_delete -f m
	doas pkg_add -u m
	pkg_check m

Documentation

	man 1 m
	https://gitlab.com/pasosdeJesus/m
	Contracts and wallet tutorial (English and Spanish), in
	doc/tutorial-contracts-openbsd-1/:
	https://gitlab.com/pasosdeJesus/m/-/tree/main/doc
